Refurbished Linux 0.3.0-r4 — a panel and wallpaper on every screen

file:   refurbished-linux-0.3.0-r4-amd64.iso
size:   824180736 bytes
sha256: b1707dd575729786022768df37dc636ded16262b3c955ec59a5136cd9cbcd821
base:   Debian 13 trixie, kernel 6.12.117-amd64, same fixes as r3

The shell opened one layer-shell bar without naming an output, so the
compositor put it on a single screen and every other monitor stayed black
and barless. It now binds each wl_output and gives each screen its own
wallpaper and its own bar, pinned to that screen.

The bar sits along the top edge like the first screen. To move every bar
to the bottom, add this to /etc/xdg/labwc/environment and log out:
  REFURB_BAR_POSITION=bottom

Verified inside the guest against a two-output compositor: the shell
reports "2 screen(s)" and creates Desktop + Bar on the first screen and
DesktopOn(1) + BarOn(1) on the second. Single-screen boot checked visually.
Not verified: a physical second monitor, and hotplugging a screen into a
running session (outputs are enumerated at startup).
